From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmp: media and playlist objects, current playlist, next/previous/playItem

Stubs (E_NOTIMPL / fake success), as documented now.

- IWMPPlaylist: the playlist keeps its items. get_Item (E_INVALIDARG out of
  range), insertItem (0..count), appendItem (it only returned S_OK before and
  forgot the item), removeItem, moveItem and clear, with reference counting
  on the items; attributeCount / attributeName / getItemInfo / setItemInfo
  with the built-in Title (the name) and ItemCount (read-only,
  E_ACCESSDENIED) and any other attribute kept as set; isIdentical.
- IWMPMedia: attributeCount / getAttributeName / getItemInfo / setItemInfo
  (built-in SourceURL, Title, Duration, then the ones that were set; SourceURL
  and Duration are read-only), isReadOnlyItem, isIdentical (same address),
  isMemberOf, markerCount (0, the files are not scanned for markers) with
  getMarkerTime / getMarkerName (E_INVALIDARG, markers count from 1),
  imageSourceWidth/Height (0), durationString (mm:ss), getItemInfoByAtom
  (E_INVALIDARG: atoms come from the media collection, which is not there).
  NULL result pointers are E_POINTER.
- IWMPPlayer4::put_currentPlaylist (E_NOTIMPL) makes the playlist the current
  one, its first item the current media, and plays it when autoStart is on;
  get_currentPlaylist returns that playlist and no longer a copy that lost
  its items. get_currentMedia's copy keeps the name and the attributes of the
  item. put_currentMedia refuses an object that is not one of this player's.
- IWMPControls::next / previous / playItem / currentItem (E_NOTIMPL):
  next/previous walk the current playlist (NS_S_WMPCORE_COMMAND_NOT_AVAILABLE
  at either end), playItem makes an item current and plays it, currentItem
  reads and sets the current media (the item has to be in the playlist);
  isAvailable("next"/"previous") follows the position.

---
